<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 8 October, from 451 to 1967.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">451 <span class="tih-ago">1,575 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Chalcedon opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bishops summoned by Emperor Marcian met at Chalcedon, across the Bosporus from Constantinople. Its definition of Christ as one person in two natures became orthodoxy in the West and Byzantium but split the eastern churches.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1856 <span class="tih-ago">170 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Chinese officials board the Arrow at Canton</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Qing officials boarded the Arrow, a Chinese-owned ship flying a British flag, and arrested its crew on suspicion of piracy. Britain used the incident as grounds for the Second Opium War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1871 <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Great Chicago Fire breaks out</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Fire broke out in a barn on DeKoven Street and, driven by strong winds, burned for two days across Chicago. About 300 people died and 100,000 lost their homes, but rebuilding made the city a centre of modern architecture.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1918 <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Corporal Alvin York captures 132 German soldiers</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the Argonne Forest, Corporal Alvin York led a small patrol that silenced German machine guns, killing about 25 soldiers and taking 132 prisoners. He received the Medal of Honor and became a national hero.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bolivia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="76" height="76"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1967 <span class="tih-ago">59 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Che Guevara is captured in Bolivia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolivian troops, aided by the CIA, wounded and captured Ernesto 'Che' Guevara in the Yuro ravine. He was executed the next day at La Higuera, and his image became an enduring icon of revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bolivia">Bolivia</a></div></div></li></ol>
